{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Mb3hSU2gw8dWzRuqngiJFi","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# N00 traceability matrix (frozen)\n2\t\n3\tEvery normative (MUST/MUST NOT/SHOULD/MAY) Plan 26 spec section, every QA\n4\tcriterion, and every adversarial case maps to exactly one owning N-node.\n5\tBuilt from spec section 19 (already-proposed mapping) plus [[node_ownership.v1]]\n6\tfor D/M-node-level detail, and cross-checked against\n7\t`implementation.graph.v2.yaml` write sets so no owner is asserted without a\n8\tcorresponding `writes` entry.\n9\t\n10\t## Spec section -> owning N-node\n11\t\n12\t| Spec section | Subject | Owning N-node |\n13\t|---|---|---|\n14\t| 0, 1 | governing decision, scope/non-goals | N00 (contract only; no code) |\n15\t| 2 | baseline assessment, reuse/adapt/replace table | N00 (baseline record); individual adaptations owned by the N-node that touches the adapted file |\n16\t| 3 | dependency/API contract | N10 |\n17\t| 4 | compiled graph ownership, one production path, `prepare_episode_invocation` | N20 (builder), N21 (`prepare_episode_invocation`), N40 (CLI sole-path enforcement) |\n18\t| 5 | typed state, reducers, persisted-state table | N11 |\n19\t| 6.1 | common node rules (idempotent replay, checkpoint boundary, guard ordering) | N22 (deterministic bodies), N23 (model bodies) |\n20\t| 6.2 | D00-D98 catalogue | per [[node_ownership.v1]] table |\n21\t| 6.3 | eight model job types | N23 |\n22\t| 7.1-7.3 | transport envelope, Codex/Gemini CLI contracts | N13 |\n23\t| 7.4 | external-data authorization | N13 |\n24\t| 8.1 | normal graph edges | N20 (skeleton), N30 (unit loop), N32 (workbook branch) |\n25\t| 8.2 | conditional-edge/guard table | N20 (`routing.py`), extended by N30/N32 registrations |\n26\t| 9 | context graph / structural isolation | N13 (workspace isolation), N23 (projection builders) |\n27\t| 10 | fan-outs/joins/correlation keys | N30 (source/visual), N32 (page review joins) |\n28\t| 11.1-11.2 | SqliteSaver, thread/namespace, dual persistence | N21, N12 (evidence layer) |\n29\t| 11.3 | graceful interruption / crash recovery | N21 (mechanics), N22 (D96 body) |\n30\t| 11.4 | resume algorithm | N21 |\n31\t| 12 | targeted repair architecture | N31 |\n32\t| 13.1 | unit denominator / acceptance | N31 |\n33\t| 13.2 | workbook denominator | N32 |\n34\t| 14 | terminal design / exit codes | N22 (`nodes/terminal.py` writer), N32 (product-terminal call sites), N40 (CLI exit-code mapping) |\n35\t| 15 | filesystem/artifact layout | N12 (artifact/evidence paths); layout resolution frozen in [[node_ownership.v1]] |\n36\t| 16 | CLI contract | N40 |\n37\t| 17.1 | test layers | every N-node owns its own layer's tests per its `writes` set; N50 owns the adversarial layer specifically |\n38\t| 17.2 | adversarial case matrix | N50 (all cases); see mapping below |\n39\t| 18 | migration/retirement boundary | N40 (cutover gates), N90 (final audit of the cutover) |\n40\t| 19 | (the spec's own traceability matrix) | superseded by this document for N-node purposes; spec section 19 remains authoritative for spec-internal cross-references |\n41\t| 20.1 | resolved decisions | N00 (already incorporated into this contract set) |\n42\t| 20.2 | external prerequisites before activation | N60 (gates `PASSED` vs `NOT_AVAILABLE`) |\n43\t| 21 | spec quality-gate checklist | N90 (final audit re-verifies every checked item against implementation, not against the spec's own self-assessment) |\n44\t\n45\t## QA criteria (`qa_criteria.v2.md`) -> owning N-node\n46\t\n47\t| Criterion | Owning N-node |\n48\t|---|---|\n49\t| reject project-management graph / handwritten controller / legacy fallback | N20, N40 (structural enforcement); N90 (final check) |\n50\t| reject LangChain/provider-SDK/HTTP model imports | N10 (forbidden-import lock check), N13 (transport), N50 (`test_no_second_production_factory`-adjacent import audit) |\n51\t| reject model-controlled routing/joins/retries/admission/acceptance/terminals | N20/N30/N31/N32 (guards remain code-owned), N50 (`test_models_have_no_control_fields`) |\n52\t| reject non-product success claims | N90 (`test_no_nonproduct_success` verified independently) |\n53\t| reject partial/duplicate/extra/stale/failed/NOT_RUN/cross-unit denominator members | N30 (source/visual joins), N32 (page joins), N50 (adversarial proof) |\n54\t| reject replay of committed external calls / mutated accepted bytes | N21, N31 |\n55\t| reject resume after drift | N21 |\n56\t| reject misuse of PAUSED_PREREQUISITE | N22 (D30 classification) |\n57\t| exact pinned dependency + API-contract tests | N10 |\n58\t| complete typed state/reducer authority and topology reports | N11, N20 |\n59\t| exactly eight model jobs, package-relative prompts/schemas | N13, N23 |\n60\t| structural model-workspace isolation + authorization before transmission | N13 |\n61\t| exact fan-out/barrier and every-page denominators | N30, N32 |\n62\t| dual checkpoint/evidence correlation + crash/resume matrix | N21, N12 |\n63\t| targeted immutable repair + accepted-unit/workbook release denominators | N31, N32 |\n64\t| one production CLI path, no legacy/simulation fallback | N40 |\n65\t| full deterministic/integration/adversarial/regression suites | every N-node (own layer) + N50 (adversarial/regression) |\n66\t| authorized live product evidence before activation, else `IMPLEMENTED_NOT_ACTIVATED` | N60, N90 |\n67\t| runtime egress enforcement | N13 |\n68\t| CI regenerates lock, fails on drift | N10 |\n69\t\n70\t## Adversarial case (section 17.2) -> verification test -> owning N-node\n71\t\n72\tAll owned by N50 (`tests/runtime/test_plan26_adversarial.py`), since that is\n73\tthe sole node whose `writes` set includes this file. N50 exercises behavior\n74\timplemented by the N-nodes named per case (source of truth for *why* the\n75\ttest should pass), but does not modify their files:\n76\t\n77\t| Case (abbreviated) | Behavior owner | Test name |\n78\t|---|---|---|\n79\t| non-product success claims | N90/N22 terminal writer | `test_no_nonproduct_success` |\n80\t| manifest-neutral dynamic run (1/7/41 units) | N22 (D02) | `test_manifest_neutral_dynamic_run` |\n81\t| model output proposes control fields | N23 schemas | `test_models_have_no_control_fields` |\n82\t| prompt resolved outside package | N13 | `test_prompts_are_package_relative` |\n83\t| malformed/multiple/trailing CLI JSON | N13 | `test_malformed_cli_output_fails_closed` |\n84\t| decided vs. executed model mismatch | N13 | `test_executed_model_must_match_route` |\n85\t| same-family reviewer | N13/N23 | `test_same_family_review_rejected` |\n86\t| exact fan-out denominator violations | N30 | `test_exact_fanout_denominators` |\n87\t| every-page review requirement | N32 | `test_every_unit_page_required`, `test_every_workbook_page_required` |\n88\t| stale hash | N31 | `test_stale_hash_rejected` |\n89\t| repair boundary/immutability | N31 | `test_repair_boundary_and_immutability` |\n90\t| local repair not whole-unit regen | N31 | `test_local_repair_is_targeted` |\n91\t| repair bound reserved before activation | N23 (D90), N31 | `test_repair_bound_reserved_first` |\n92\t| resume preserves accepted bytes | N21 | `test_resume_preserves_accepted_bytes` |\n93\t| duplicate continuation prevented | N21 | `test_duplicate_continuation_prevented` |\n94\t| workbook exact manifest coverage | N32 | `test_workbook_exact_manifest_coverage` |\n95\t| workbook repair cannot change unit | N32 | `test_workbook_repair_cannot_change_unit` |\n96\t| no second production factory | N40 | `test_no_second_production_factory` |\n97\t| external-data authorization precedes transmission | N13 | `test_external_data_authorization_precedes_transmission` |\n98\t| worker context structurally bounded | N13 | `test_worker_context_is_structurally_bounded` |\n99\t| dual persistence correlation | N21/N12 | `test_dual_persistence_correlation` |\n100\t| resume bootstrap skips fresh write-once nodes | N21/N22 | `test_resume_bootstrap_skips_fr