{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0168kHQVbM95foaaANYNST3K","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# N40_CLI_CUTOVER result\n2\t\n3\tstatus: PASSED\n4\tnode_prompt: plans/26_langgraph_curriculum_factory/prompts/N40_cli_cutover.prompt.v1.md\n5\tpredecessor: N32_WORKBOOK_TERMINALS (compact state supplied by the controller, status PASSED)\n6\tgeneration: 2\n7\t\n8\t## Generation 2 correction (patch P-N40-001)\n9\t\n10\t**What was wrong.** Generation 1's own \"Migration disposition\" section (below,\n11\tpreserved) already disclosed that `tests/runtime/test_run_curriculum.py`\n12\ttested the retired Plan 25 surface — `from runtime.run_curriculum import\n13\tmain, parser_for`, `parser_for(runtime)`, and a `--lab-id` dispatch mocking\n14\t`runtime.run_curriculum.CurriculumFactoryGraph`/`CodexWorker` — and that this\n15\tbroke collection of `tests/runtime` for `pytest -q tests/runtime`. The file\n16\twas outside this node's write set in generation 1, so it could not be fixed.\n17\t\n18\t**Why this node owns it.** The write set was corrected to include\n19\t`tests/runtime/test_run_curriculum.py`: it is this node's own CLI cutover\n20\tthat made the file's assertions stale, so this node retires/rewrites them\n21\trather than leaving a downstream node to route around a collection-blocking\n22\timport error it did not cause.\n23\t\n24\t**What changed.** `tests/runtime/test_run_curriculum.py`'s\n25\t`RunCurriculumParserTests` class (and its shared `from runtime.run_curriculum\n26\timport main, parser_for` import) was replaced with\n27\t`RunCurriculumMigrationContractTests`, asserting the Plan 26 migration\n28\tcontract instead of the removed Plan 25 dispatch behavior:\n29\t- `parser_for` is absent from `runtime.run_curriculum` (`hasattr` is false;\n30\t  `from runtime.run_curriculum import parser_for` raises `ImportError`).\n31\t- The current `build_parser()` rejects every legacy flag the old parser\n32\t  accepted (`--lab-id`, `--max-model-calls-per-lab`, `--max-concurrency`,\n33\t  `--max-meta-revision-cycles`, `--retry-malformed-output`) with\n34\t  `SystemExit(2)`.\n35\t- A static AST scan of `runtime/run_curriculum.py` (consistent with the\n36\t  import-audit style in `tests/runtime/test_plan26_cli.py`) asserts no Plan 25\n37\t  symbol (`CurriculumFactoryGraph`, `CodexWorker`, `GeminiReviewer`,\n38\t  `CurriculumRuntime`, `parser_for`) or module (`runtime.controller`,\n39\t  `runtime.session_bridge`, `runtime.curriculum_factory_graph`,\n40\t  `runtime.model_worker`) is referenced or imported.\n41\t\n42\t`RunCurriculumElapsedTimeTests` — which drives `runtime.controller\n43\t.CurriculumRuntime.simulate(...)` directly, a historical module deliberately\n44\tleft in place and unreachable from the production CLI — was left untouched\n45\texcept for the shared top-of-file import no longer naming `parser_for`.\n46\tNeither `runtime/run_curriculum.py` nor `tests/runtime/test_plan26_cli.py`\n47\tnor `tests/runtime/test_plan26_workbook.py` were modified (hashes below are\n48\tunchanged from generation 1). Verified with:\n49\t\n50\t```\n51\t{python} -m pytest -q tests/runtime/test_plan26_cli.py tests/runtime/test_plan26_workbook.py tests/runtime/test_run_curriculum.py\n52\t# 76 passed, 14 subtests passed\n53\t```\n54\t\n55\t## What this node built\n56\t\n57\t- `runtime/run_curriculum.py` — rewritten from the Plan 25 `CurriculumRuntime`/\n58\t  `CurriculumFactoryGraph`/`CodexWorker` dispatcher into the sole production CLI\n59\t  described by spec section 16. It parses/validates the exact\n60\t  preflight/`--unit`/`--all`/`--resume` argument surface, canonicalizes\n61\t  `--engine-root`/`--curriculum`/`--output-root`, enforces the fresh-run\n62\t  collision rule and the resume-identity rule, acquires the per-output-root\n63\t  execution lock, calls `persistence.prepare_episode_invocation` once, builds\n64\t  `runtime.langgraph_factory.graph.build_curriculum_factory_graph` exactly once\n65\t  per execution path, invokes it, projects the returned `FactoryOutput` into the\n66\t  one printed JSON object, and maps the result to spec section 14's exit codes.\n67\t  It holds no node body, no guard, no join, no acceptance rule, and no frontier\n68\t  selection.\n69\t- `tests/runtime/test_plan26_cli.py` — 72 tests covering the node's own TEST\n70\t  checklist (below).\n71\t- `results/evidence/N40_CLI_CUTOVER/` — `focused_test_run.txt` (this node's exact\n72\t  verification command), `cli_help.txt` and `import_audit.txt` (regenerated by\n73\t  tests, not hand-written), `preflight_read_only.txt` and\n74\t  `plan25_resume_refusal.txt` (real, unmocked runs of `main()` against a real\n75\t  filesystem, captured as a test side effect so they can never drift from what\n76\t  actually passed).\n77\t\n78\t## Migration disposition\n79\t\n80\tThe GOAL explicitly allows historical modules to remain \"only when unreachable\n81\tfrom the production import/call graph.\" `runtime/run_curriculum.py` no longer\n82\timports `runtime.controller.CurriculumRuntime`, `runtime.curriculum_factory_graph\n83\t.CurriculumFactoryGraph`, `runtime.model_worker.CodexWorker`/`GeminiReviewer`, or\n84\t`runtime.session_bridge` — the entire Plan 25 dispatcher, the custom FSM\n85\t(`controller.simulate`), and the session bridge are all unreachable from the one\n86\tproduction entry point now. Those modules, and their own dedicated tests\n87\t(`tests/runtime/test_controller.py`, `test_curriculum_factory_graph.py`), are\n88\tleft in place as readable history, per the GOAL's \"do not delete user history.\"\n89\t\n90\t**One residual conflict, out of this node's write set.**\n91\t`tests/runtime/test_run_curriculum.py` is not in this node's declared writable\n92\tpaths and could not be touched. It tests the *old* `run_curriculum.parser_for`/\n93\t`main` API directly — mocking `runtime.run_curriculum.CurriculumFactoryGraph`\n94\tand asserting a `--lab-id` dispatch to `factory.run(...)`. That is precisely the\n95\tPlan 25 fallback path this node's GOAL requires removing, so the file now fails\n96\tto import (`cannot import name 'parser_for'`) against the new CLI. This node's\n97\town verification command\n98\t(`{python} -m pytest -q tests/runtime/test_plan26_cli.py\n99\ttests/runtime/test_plan26_workbook.py`) does not exercise that file and passes\n100\tcleanly; `pytest -q tests/runtime` (run by N50, per\n101\t`implementation.graph.v3.yaml`) will fail collection on it until a node with\n102\twrite access to `tests/runtime/test_run_curriculum.py` retires or rewrites it.\n103\tFlagging this explicitly rather than routing around it silently.\n104\t\n105\t**Graph topology inherited, not extended.** `build_curriculum_factory_graph`\n106\t(`runtime/langgraph_factory/graph.py`, sha256\n107\t`eae00c21bfe55ce6e2d6c4374611db4d84d286218d498fa520e799288e152e26`, unchanged —\n108\tmatches N32's own receipted output hash exactly) wires the skeleton and the\n109\tper-unit fan-out path only; the unit-repair cycle (D16-D23) and the workbook\n110\tengine (D24-D32, `register_workbook_topology`) are not yet wired into the one\n111\tcompile point `binding_inventory()`'s own docstring documents this as N31's/\n112\tN32's deliberate deferral, not a regression this node introduced. `graph.py` is\n113\tnot in this node's write set, so a live run that reaches an unwired destination\n114\traises `KeyError`; the CLI's top-level `except Exception` catches it and prints\n115\ta `SYSTEM_FAILURE`-shaped object with exit 20, never a fabricated success. This\n116\tis the correct, honest behavior for the graph's current state, not a workaround.\n117\t\n118\t## TEST checklist, item by item\n119\t\n120\t1. **Static and runtime call-graph proof shows one production graph\n121\t   builder/path.** `ImportGraphAuditTests` parses the CLI's own AST and asserts\n122\t   no Plan 25/legacy module or symbol is imported, and that\n123\t   `build_curriculum_factory_graph` is the only builder referenced (no\n124\t   `register_skeleton`