t   and never `UNIT_ACCEPTED`/`COMPLETE`, and a preflight against a non-empty\n151\t   root reports the collision without touching a byte of it.\n152\t5. **CLI code contains no product nodes, guards, joins, acceptance, or\n153\t   frontier selection.** `test_no_product_node_or_guard_identifiers_appear_in_source`\n154\t   regex-scans the entire file for any `D\\d\\d*`/`M0[1-8]*` token and asserts\n155\t   none exist; `test_only_two_narrow_pure_helpers_are_imported_from_nodes_inputs`\n156\t   and `test_no_import_from_any_other_nodes_or_routing_or_workbook_module` pin\n157\t   the one declared exception (see below) and reject every other import from\n158\t   `nodes.*`, `routing`, `workbook`, `unit_graph`, `model_nodes`, `repair`.\n159\t6. **Missing authorization/capability fails before transmission and never\n160\t   simulates.** `CapabilityAndAuthorizationFailureTests` monkeypatches\n161\t   `transport.prove_transport_capabilities` to raise and asserts the stub\n162\t   compiled graph's `invoke` is **never called**, the process exits 20, and the\n163\t   printed `terminal.kind` is `SYSTEM_FAILURE`; a missing `--authorization`\n164\t   file fails before `build_curriculum_factory_graph` is even called (exit 2,\n165\t   no `terminal` key at all — never a fabricated one).\n166\t7. **Existing Plan 25 roots are readable history but refused for Plan 26\n167\t   resume.** `Plan25ResumeRefusalTests` builds a `checkpoints/0001.json`-shaped\n168\t   legacy root (no `.langgraph/`), runs `--resume` against it, and asserts the\n169\t   graph builder is never called, exit is 3, and the root's file set and bytes\n170\t   are **byte-identical** before and after — the identity-envelope check\n171\t   (`P.read_identity_envelope`) runs before the execution lock is even\n172\t   acquired, so a doomed resume leaves zero filesystem footprint. See\n173\t   `results/evidence/N40_CLI_CUTOVER/plan25_resume_refusal.txt`.\n174\t8. **Production import audit rejects LangChain wrappers/provider SDKs/direct\n175\t   model HTTP.** `test_no_langchain_provider_sdk_or_direct_http_imports`\n176\t   scans every import in the file against `langchain`, `openai`, `anthropic`,\n177\t   `google.generativeai`, `requests`, `httpx`, `urllib3`; none appear. The\n178\t   full, regenerated import list is `results/evidence/N40_CLI_CUTOVER/import_audit.txt`\n179\t   (20 imports total, all stdlib or `runtime.langgraph_factory.*`).\n180\t\n181\t## The one declared exception to \"no node-body imports\"\n182\t\n183\t`_resolve_active_manifest` and `_frozen_input_records`\n184\t(`runtime.langgraph_factory.nodes.inputs`) are imported and called once each,\n185\tbefore the graph exists, to fix the identity seed\n186\t(`persistence.prepare_episode_invocation`'s `active_manifest_path`) and the\n187\tauthorization/transport `curriculum_digest` a `RuntimeContext` needs before its\n188\tfirst invocation. Both are pure, side-effect-free hashing/selection functions —\n189\tnot a node body, not a guard, not a routing or acceptance decision. The graph's\n190\town input-freezing node independently recomputes the same values inside the\n191\tepisode and is the sole authority the graph trusts; a drift between the CLI's\n192\tpre-computed digest and the graph's own recomputed one fails closed (an\n193\tauthorization/curriculum-digest mismatch), it never succeeds silently. Reusing\n194\tthe functions, rather than re-implementing the hashing rule a second time, is\n195\twhat keeps the two computations from silently drifting apart.\n196\t\n197\t## Commands\n198\t\n199\t```\n200\t{python} -m pytest -q tests/runtime/test_plan26_cli.py tests/runtime/test_plan26_workbook.py\n201\t# 72 passed\n202\t```\n203\t\n204\t## Hashes\n205\t\n206\t| Path | sha256 |\n207\t|---|---|\n208\t| `runtime/run_curriculum.py` | `76da9110121ede62a64f29585b840ac934828b41a6376831a355fa95519ec170` |\n209\t| `tests/runtime/test_plan26_cli.py` | `8d627b17176fb761c765aa32b8c0804958920335b15ee4b273731f9884f58f46` |\n210\t| `runtime/lan