{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01B1TeWYSNrERVr53yAxja3Z","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# N00 digest algorithm (frozen)\n2\t\n3\tBinds every later hash reference used by result records, receipts, and the\n4\tscheduler's predecessor/result-hash bookkeeping.\n5\t\n6\t## File digest\n7\t\n8\t`SHA-256` over raw file bytes, no normalization, computed with\n9\t`hashlib.sha256(path.read_bytes()).hexdigest()` in code and\n10\t`shasum -a 256 <path>` for manual verification. Text files are hashed as\n11\tcommitted (repo `.gitattributes` defines line-ending policy; digests are not\n12\trecomputed after checkout-time normalization).\n13\t\n14\t## Graph digest\n15\t\n16\t`graph_digest = sha256(implementation.graph.v2.yaml raw bytes)`. Any edit to\n17\tthe graph (including whitespace) changes the digest and invalidates every\n18\tscheduler receipt that cited the prior value. The schema file\n19\t(`implementation.graph.schema.v2.json`) is validated but not folded into the\n20\tgraph digest; its own digest is recorded separately in receipts that perform\n21\tschema validation.\n22\t\n23\t## Canonical JSON digest (state, receipts, records)\n24\t\n25\tFor any persisted structured record (result records' embedded data, artifact\n26\tversion records, evidence entries, checkpoint-correlation entries):\n27\t\n28\t1. Serialize with `json.dumps(obj, sort_keys=True, ensure_ascii=False,\n29\t   separators=(\",\", \":\"))`.\n30\t2. UTF-8 encode.\n31\t3. `sha256` the bytes.\n32\t\n33\tThis is the one canonical-JSON rule for the whole Plan 26 implementation;\n34\tnode prompts MUST NOT invent a second serialization convention. `NaN`,\n35\t`Infinity`, and non-finite floats are forbidden inputs (fail closed before\n36\tserialization) because they are not round-trip-stable JSON.\n37\t\n38\t## Content-addressed artifact paths\n39\t\n40\tWhere the spec (section 15) stores an artifact under a `<hash>` path segment,\n41\tthe hash is the file digest (raw bytes) of that exact artifact, not a\n42\tcanonical-JSON digest of a wrapping record.\n43\t\n44\t## Result-record command/exit-code capture\n45\t\n46\tA result record's `commands` entries capture the literal invoked command\n47\tstring and integer exit code; a command's stdout/stderr are captured to the\n48\tevidence path referenced from the record, not inlined, when they exceed 4 KiB.\n49\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0307cd11-8c01-4a45-8d2f-da74afa560e3","uuid":"2d737536-1b6c-4f4c-bb39-67904f7220b7","timestamp":"2026-08-13T00:32:37.097Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/filipepinto/Projects/curriculum_builder/.plan26-run/plan26/attempts/N90_FINAL_AUDIT/attempt-20260813T002841.066117Z-baf3aca859/repo/plans/26_langgraph_curriculum_factory/contracts/digest_algorithm.v1.md","content":"# N00 digest algorithm (frozen)\n\nBinds every later hash reference used by result records, receipts, and the\nscheduler's predecessor/result-hash bookkeeping.\n\n## File digest\n\n`SHA-256` over raw file bytes, no normalization, computed with\n`hashlib.sha256(path.read_bytes()).hexdigest()` in code and\n`shasum -a 256 <path>` for manual verification. Text files are hashed as\ncommitted (repo `.gitattributes` defines line-ending policy; digests are not\nrecomputed after checkout-time normalization).\n\n## Graph digest\n\n`graph_digest = sha256(implementation.graph.v2.yaml raw bytes)`. Any edit to\nthe graph (including whitespace) changes the digest and invalidates every\nscheduler receipt that cited the prior value. The schema file\n(`implementation.graph.schema.v2.json`) is validated but not folded into the\ngraph digest; its own digest is recorded separately in receipts that perform\nschema validation.\n\n## Canonical JSON digest (state, receipts, records)\n\nFor any persisted structured record (result records' embedded data, artifact\nversion records, evidence entries, checkpoint-correlation entries):\n\n1. Serialize with `json.dumps(obj, sort_keys=True, ensure_ascii=False,\n   separators=(\",\", \":\"))`.\n2. UTF-8 encode.\n3. `sha256` the bytes.\n\nThis is the one canonical-JSON rule for the whole Plan 26 implementation;\nnode prompts MUST NOT invent a second serialization convention. `NaN`,\n`Infinity`, and non-finite floats are forbidden inputs (fail closed before\nserialization) because they are not round-trip-stable JSON.\n\n## Content-addressed artifact paths\n\nWhere the spec (section 15) stores an artifact under a `<hash>` path segment,\nthe hash is the file digest (raw bytes) of that exact artifact, not a\ncanonical-JSON digest of a wrapping record.\n\n## Result-record command/exit-code capture\n\nA result record's `commands` entries capture the literal invoked command\nstring and integer exit code; a command's stdout/stderr are captured to the\nevidence path referenced from the record, not inlined, when they exceed 4 KiB.\n","numLines":49,"startLine":1,"totalLines":49}}}
