` JSON payload, which\nincludes `output_root`, `persistence.output_root`, and `logger.evidence_root`\npaths built from `tempfile`'s randomized directory names (e.g.\n`/private/var/.../tmpi9hqmb3c/preflight-target`,\n`/private/var/.../plan26-preflight-ystqattw`). These paths differ on every\ntest invocation, so the evidence directory's content — and therefore its\nsha256 digest — can never reproduce the value captured at receipt time,\nregardless of whether any code changed.\n\nConfirmed byte-for-byte: `import_audit.txt`, `cli_help.txt`,\n`plan25_resume_refusal.txt` are stable/deterministic; only\n`preflight_read_only.txt`'s embedded tempdir paths vary between runs.\n\nLive consequence (reproduced against the controller's own `status`\nsubcommand, not just this manual check — see controller_status.json in this\nsame evidence directory):\n\n  \"stale_receipts\": [\"N40_CLI_CUTOVER\"]\n  \"statuses\": {\n    ...\n    \"N40_CLI_CUTOVER\": \"READY\",       <- was PASSED; controller now wants to rerun it\n    \"N50_ADVERSARIAL_REGRESSION\": \"PENDING\",  <- cascaded from N40\n    \"N60_LIVE_PRODUCT_PROOF\": \"PENDING\",      <- cascaded from N50\n    \"N90_FINAL_AUDIT\": \"PENDING\"\n  }\n\nThis is a real, currently-active cascade in the graph's own admissibility\nlogic (`ScheduleState.admissible()` walks every ancestor's declared\n`outputs`, including evidence directories, and rejects reuse on any digest\nmismatch — `prompt_graph_controller.py:729-794`). It is not an artifact of\nthis audit's own commands: the mismatch was present before any pytest command\nwas run in this N90 session (first observed via a plain hash comparison\nbefore the first `pytest` invocation of this session), and running the full\nsuite again (as N50's own mandated verification command does) reliably\nreproduces/re-triggers it, because `test_plan26_cli.py` is always part of\nthat command.\n\nDisposition: reported to N90 as the sole blocking finding of this audit pass,\nrouted via `rework_edges.cli